477	 * still hash to the same {@code <REGION>-<HASH8>}. When the computed code collides with an
478	 * existing owner's {@code customerCode}, {@code -<n>} is appended with the smallest
479	 * {@code n} of 2 or more that makes it unique. The new owner is not yet saved, so it is
480	 * not among the existing owners scanned here.
